{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And Balak said to him: Come now with me, etc.</b> The word <b>נָא</b>, and also <b>וקבנו לי</b> in a definitive mood, will be explained according to the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Numbers Rabbah 20) who said that he saw that Israel were breached there, where Moses died, end quote. This is because he did not know the reason for the breach, so he thought the breach would persist among them. And since Israel were known to do repentance and annul decrees, he hastened to say <b>לך נא</b> — meaning, hurry now, for I see that they are held liable for this breach, before they do repentance. <b>וקבנו לי</b> — he finalized the certainty of the matter, that curses would overtake them, O wicked one."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:13:11.191409112Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}